---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMPANY, PRIVACY_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Cookie policy · ChalkPis Tutor" description="Which cookies chalkpistutor.com uses and how to change your choice.">
  <article class="wrap sec end legal">
    <h1 class="h2">Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="body">
      This website, chalkpistutor.com, is run by {COMPANY}. It uses a few cookies and similar browser storage to learn
      which pages are useful and which ads bring people here. The ChalkPis Tutor app and sign-up pages on
      tutor.chalkpis.com do not use these tools.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4">What we use</h2>
    <ul class="body">
      <li>
        <strong>Your cookie choice.</strong> Saved in your browser so we don't ask on every page. Always on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics.</strong> Counts visits, pages viewed and steps such as tapping "Start free trial". Before
        you choose, or if you reject, it sends visit counts without cookies. If you accept, it sets its own cookies
        (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>), kept for up to 14 months.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meta Pixel.</strong> Tells Meta (Facebook and Instagram) when a visit from one of our ads leads to a
        sign-up, so we can see which ads work. It runs only if you choose "Accept all", and sets the <code>_fbp</code>
        cookie, kept for up to 90 days.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body">
      We never send your name, phone number or email to these tools. How we handle the details you give when you sign
      up is in our <a href={PRIVACY_URL}>Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4">Changing your choice</h2>
    <p class="body">
      <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>Change your cookie choice</a> at any time, or clear this site's data in your
      browser. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="small">Last updated 5 November 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 720px; }
  .legal h2 { margin: 40px 0 0; }
  .legal p, .legal ul { margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .legal a { color: var(--blue); }
  .legal code { font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
